 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by the retry helper raising a generic 'retries exhausted' error instead of re-raising the original exception. The fix captures the last caught exception during retries and re-raises it when all attempts are exhausted, preserving the original error message. This ensures that the error context is maintained even after the retry limit is reached.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/retry.py b/tracker/retry.py\nindex 0e5bdcb..d4409ba 100644\n--- a/tracker/retry.py\n+++ b/tracker/retry.py\n@@ -22,9 +22,10 @@ def retry_call(func, attempts=3, base_delay=0.05, sleep=time.sleep, retry_on=(Tr\n         raise ValueError(\"attempts must be >= 1\")\n     delays = backoff_delays(attempts, base_delay)\n     for attempt in range(attempts):\n-        try:\n-            return func()\n-        except retry_on:\n-            if attempt == attempts - 1:\n-                raise TransientError(\"retries exhausted\")\n-            sleep(delays[attempt])\n+            try:\n+                return func()\n+            except retry_on as e:\n+                if attempt == attempts - 1:\n+                    last_exception = e\n+                    raise\n+                sleep(delays[attempt])\n",
